Changes include an OpenClaw tool adapter and a parser/engine redesign using
file-record parsing, ordered edit operations, source-offset references, candidate
ranking, and a piece-table edit plan. Better Patch adds source-context retention,
line-ending inference, ambiguity rejection, anchored insertions, and
content-independent idempotent deletion. Codex environment routing, streaming
execution, exec-server integration, and approval machinery are not included.
The redesign is not represented as a clean-room implementation or as a finding
that upstream attribution obligations have ended.
